# Environments
.env
# Dotenv variants (.env.local, .env.production, ...) and private key
# material. The bare `.env` line does not match a suffixed file, and a key
# committed to a repository that is intended to become public is published
# the moment visibility changes.
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
.venv
# Version-suffixed virtualenvs (.venv311, venv312, ...). The bare `.venv` and
# `venv/` lines above do not match them, so a dev environment in the repository
# root was untracked but not ignored -- one `git add -A` away from being
# committed into a repository that is intended to become public.
.venv*/
venv*/
env/
venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

